rab@comp.rgu.ac.uk wrote:

>> You will revert to human eventually, or sooner if you reach 0
>> hitpoints. If you want to revert sooner rather than later try
>> throwing daggers straight up.
> 
> Thanks very much - I tried it and it worked perfectly (just two throws
> of an arrow, as I didn't have a dagger to hand).  Sorry if my question
> was a FAQ, but the fact that you revert to human at 0HP rather than
> dying was a total surprise; I hadn't come across it in any of the many
> nethack spoiler documents. 

It may have been a surprise, but most unspoiled players find out pretty 
quickly that they revert to human form as soon as their hitpoints reach 
zero (especially if they managed to polymorph into a newt or similar 
useless creature).

OTOH, the polymorph spoiler seems pretty clear:
http://www.spod-central.org/%7Epsmith/nh/wan2-343.txt

> How long you are polymorphed depends on your experience level and the
> level of the monster you became (this prevents abuse by low-level
> characters); you will not revert while you have unchanging.  You can
> always return to your natural form by losing all of your hit points
> (in a pinch by throwing objects upwards (<) and letting them hit you)
> unless you have unchanging; in this case, you will simply die.  Other
> monsters remain the same species indefinitely (except true
> shapeshifters). 



